  "title": "The soft D",
  "summary_es": {
    "en": "Between vowels “d” is soft: cansado, comido, nada.",
    "fr": "Entre voyelles, « d » est doux : cansado, comido, nada.",
    "zh": "元音之间的 d 很轻：cansado, comido, nada。",
    "ja": "母音にはさまれた d は弱くなります：cansado, comido, nada。"
  },
  "focus": "endings",
  "sounds": [
    "ð"
  ],
  "tip_es": "Between vowels, and at the end of a word, “d” is soft, like the “th” in English “this”, but very light: nada, comido, ciudad. Do not say a hard English “d”. In -ado endings it often almost disappears in speech: cansado sounds like “cansao”.",
